From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:22:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 64/72] fix(gastown): require the refinery as assignee before
 reading a bead as submitted (gcp-0pa4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mol-polecat-work's `submit-and-exit` already-submitted guard, and both
prompt-side copies of the same check, treated "the work bead's assignee is
somebody other than this session" as proof that the refinery handoff had
happened. It never asked whether that somebody WAS the refinery. Any third
identity a work bead can land on satisfies the test: an operator parking it on
a crew seat, a witness re-routing it, a reviewer taking it. A resuming polecat
then announces ALREADY_SUBMITTED, drains, and the refinery never receives the
work while the branch sits on origin unmerged. Observed in production on
winnow-zgr2y.8 (parked on winnow/specialists.thomas); field report winnow-zmjqd.
Blast radius grows with every parked seat holding an open bead.

The mark of a completed handoff is now an IDENTITY test against the value the
handoff actually writes. `submit-and-exit` step 8 sets
`assignee = ${GC_RIG:+$GC_RIG/}<binding_prefix>refinery`, so the guard resolves
`REFINERY_TARGET` with that exact expression — in its own fenced block, since an
agent may run each block in a fresh shell and an inherited-empty REFINERY_TARGET
would silently degrade the check into "assignee is empty", which never fires.
Everything else about the guard is unchanged: the other two marks (metadata.target
recorded, branch on origin at this commit) still have to hold together with it,
and no positive evidence still means fall through and run the handoff.

In the prompt template and the approval-fallacy fragment this subsumes the
predecessor-session escape gcp-5gir added one commit earlier. That escape existed
because a pool restart mints a new session identity, so a resumed molecule finds
its own previous session still holding the bead — which "assigned to somebody
else" wrongly read as a handoff. Testing for the refinery directly excludes a
predecessor session and every other non-refinery identity by construction, so
WORK_SESSION_TAG and its metadata.polecat_session read are gone from these two
blocks. `polecat_session` itself is untouched and still load-bearing for the
witness's worktree reaper and the resume re-verify; the formula prose now says so
precisely rather than naming the done sequence as a third reader.

Validation: the three new pins in test_gastown_pack_assets.sh were driven
red→green. Against the pre-fix tree they fail with "must require the work bead to
be held by the refinery, not merely by somebody other than this session"; against
a tree fixed everywhere except the guard-local REFINERY_TARGET resolve they fail
with "must resolve REFINERY_TARGET in its own block rather than inherit it".
gcp-5gir's own regression pin is restated on the stronger invariant rather than
dropped. All 11 gastown shell suites pass, `go test .` passes, registry validation
passes, and a Go text/template harness renders the composed polecat prompt to
confirm `{{ .BindingPrefix }}` resolves inside a fragment (no fragment used that
field before this commit) — both copies emit
REFINERY_TARGET="${GC_RIG:+$GC_RIG/}gastown.refinery".
